  "_note": "tengu_* event names in registration order: api (25) -> agent (30) -> session (19) -> tool (134) -> cost (10) -> oauth (8) -> memory (12) -> settings (3). Tail counts already reconciled through the 2026-09-01 session-persistence pass (registry 396). This MCP parity pass appends 20 more provider-neutral, non-deferred `tengu_mcp_*` analytics names at the MCP tail block end, growing `telemetry::tengu::mcp::NAMES` from 24 to 44 and the global registry from 396 to 416 while preserving append-only order. Authoritative exact-source audit against the local Claude Code 2.1.252 oracle confirms 65 `tengu_mcp_*` analytics names total; 10 are excluded from provider-neutral parity (6 first-party/IDE plus 4 channel), leaving 55 relevant names. This fixture now pins 44 of those 55 names. The exact remaining 11 are `instructions_pool_change`, `dropped_tools_pool_change`, `skills_funnel`, `arg_trailing_invoke_suffix`, `description_contains_toolcall_xml`, `dialog_choice`, `multidialog_choice`, `proxy_needs_approval_retry`, `registry_fetch`, `sdk_generation`, and `tripwire`. The 2.1.263 teammate pass removes the six obsolete explicit team-tool lifecycle events, leaving 410 entries. Do not read registry presence as proof that every caller is already wired.",
